(R/'README.md').write_text(f'''# AxilDB dark mode design audit\n\nOpen [visual-review.html](visual-review.html) in a browser. Keep this entire directory together; all images and scripts are local. No server or internet is required for review.\n\nSource: `{commit}` · application {raw['version']} · captured {raw['capturedAt']}. Audit only: production code, schemas, preferences and real records were not changed. No Web or host deployment is required.\n\n100 route templates captured at desktop and mobile widths; 96 initial-state reviews, 3 redirect aliases and 1 unavailable sitter interior. 62 additional current, proposed, annotated and light-reference views. {len(inv['components'])} component files source-scanned; that is not a claim of full runtime coverage.\n\nFindings: {counts}. P1 includes four opaque computed contrast failures and two gradient candidates with localized painted confirmation. P2 focus finding has no claimed conformance ratio. No blanket accessibility certification. The source revision must be revalidated if the application changes before implementation.\n\nReview controls save decisions in this browser only. Export JSON or Markdown to retain decisions; nothing is sent to AxilDB. Export before moving to another browser. File-browser storage may be unavailable, so export remains the durable record.\n\n- [Executive summary](executive-summary.md)\n- [Findings](findings.md) and [machine-readable findings](findings.json)\n- [Coverage](coverage.json), [theme inventory](theme-inventory.md), [source inventory](source-inventory.json)\n- [Palette proposals](proposed-palette.md), [implementation roadmap](implementation-roadmap.md)\n- [Computed contrast samples](contrast-measurements.json), [localized painted samples](painted-measurements.json)\n\n## Limitations\n\n{limitations}\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTools under `tools/` are audit utilities, not production services. They assume a disposable local PostgreSQL database on port 55441 named `axildb_dark_audit`, existing built application on port 3107, and temporary credentials at `/tmp/axildb-dark-audit-context.json`. Seed-base guards against a different database URL. Run only against a clean disposable database; do not point at production. Fixtures use fictional records and no providers or workers. Capture blocks mutations and external HTTP. The component harness renders production components statically; behavior is not exercised. Temporary credentials are deliberately absent from this package.\n\nCapture route defaults with `node tools/capture.mjs`, additional states with `node tools/extra-captures.mjs`, and painted samples with `node tools/painted-measurements.mjs` from the repository root using the full audit tool paths. `build-report.py` consumes the temporary raw capture files, which are not retained in this portable package. Re-capture recreates them.\n''')
(R/'executive-summary.md').write_text(f'''# Executive summary\n\nAudit of `{commit}`. No production implementation or deployment performed.\n\nThe most urgent confirmed failures are activity labels at 1.10–1.17:1, backup-storage text at 1.14:1, primary action labels at 4.02:1 and secondary approval labels at 3.47:1. Repair the shared action pair and literal light surfaces first. Care overdue and location metadata also need attention; their gradient estimates are explicitly distinguished from opaque measurements.\n\nSeverity counts: {counts}. No P0 was established. Findings count design issues, not every failing DOM element. Disabled controls, color emoji and intentional light/print views are not counted as dark-mode failures.\n\nRecommend direction B, botanical charcoal, as a review starting point: clearer solid surfaces, botanical accents and consistent action/focus roles. A preserves the established warm olive character with targeted fixes; C is the more neutral alternative. All are browser-injected demonstrations, not implementation-ready or fully certified themes.\n\nCoverage: 100 route templates, desktop 1440×900 and mobile 390×844; 96 initial-state reviews, 3 redirects, one sitter interior gap. Additional views cover a cadence dialog, expanded instance details, login focus, viewer mobile access, deployment-state fixtures, shared controls, photo framing, chart and semantic palettes. Preserve the successful shared care/tag color pairs and intentional light marketing/public/print exceptions.\n\n{limitations}\n''')
(R/'findings.md').write_text('# Findings\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f"## {f['id']} · {f['severity']} · {f['title']}\n\n{f['problem']}\n\nProposed: {f['proposal']}\n\nAcceptance: {f['acceptance']}\n\nSource: `{f['source']}`\n\n[Current evidence]({f['current']})\n\nMeasurement: {json.dumps(f['measurement']) if f['measurement'] else 'Design/source observation, no numeric contrast claim.'}" for f in F))
(R/'theme-inventory.md').write_text(f'''# Theme and component inventory\n\nSource `{commit}`. Systematic scan: {len(inv['files'])} implementation files, {len(inv['components'])} component files. Full file/line literal-color inventory and nonvisual API routes are in source-inventory.json. API routes are outside visual screenshot scope.\n\nTheme ownership: app/globals.css provides light/dark variables and compatibility selectors. app/layout.tsx sets the root theme early; ThemeToggle reads and persists axildb-theme. ForceLightTheme intentionally presents public/marketing views in light mode and restores the preferred root state without changing the preference. Print/export surfaces must preserve paper backgrounds.\n\nCurrent dark theme: forest canvas #0f160f, solid surface #1e251b, ivory text #eee7d7, heading #fff3dc, muted #bdb5a5, accent #9bc38a. Translucent surfaces and a warm gradient require measuring actual compositing. Compatibility mappings contain {inv['importantDeclarations']} !important declarations; literal matches miss new hues and opacity variants.\n\nShared care-category and plant-tag tokens have explicit paired dark foreground/background/border roles. Their isolated palette fixture looks coherent; preserve category names and icons. Shared controls, cards, tables and forms are present in real route captures. Deployment progress (running/error/complete), photo framing, chart and disabled/read-only controls also have isolated static fixtures. Dialog runtime captured through care-cadence editing; login keyboard focus captured.\n\nNo blanket sign-off for every tooltip, dropdown, portal, toast, loading skeleton, native select, chart series, server error, upgrade state or responsive permission combination. Per-route coverage records default captures and gaps; source scan is evidence of inventory, not interaction coverage.\n\nLight references are captured for dashboard, grid, cadence section, care queue and backup storage. Intentional public/print light surfaces remain outside dark remediation; follow-up implementation must regression-test these boundaries.\n''')
(R/'proposed-palette.md').write_text('# Proposed palettes — demonstrations only\n\nA retains current warm forest/ivory foundations and demonstrates paired status colors, darker action fill and visible focus. B uses botanical charcoal with solid layered surfaces; recommended for review. C uses neutral charcoal with botanical accents. None has been implemented in AxilDB.\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join('## '+k+'\n\n| Role | Proposed value |\n|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f'| `{key}` | `{value}` |' for key,value in p.items())for k,p in states['palettes'].items())+'\n\nBrowser-injected CSS is retained in assets/proposed-treatments.css for traceability. It contains successive direction blocks for documentation; do not load the whole file into production. Shared demo corrections are deliberately broad and need component-level implementation, interaction testing and measured contrast before approval. Untreated comparison views may retain defects. Color remains supplemental to text, icon and state labels.\n')
(R/'implementation-roadmap.md').write_text('''# Proposed implementation roadmap\n\nNo phase below is authorized by completion of this audit; review decisions first.\n\n1. **Accessibility foundation:** DM-003, DM-004, DM-008. Define distinct accent foreground, action background, focus, status foreground/background, surface, elevated and inset roles. Measure pairs in both themes and keyboard interaction. Keep disabled states separate from actionable controls.\n2. **Visible failures:** DM-001, DM-002, DM-005, DM-006. Replace literals at their owning components. Confirm actual painted backgrounds for translucent candidates; test loading/error/unavailable and empty states.\n3. **Semantic review and consolidation:** DM-007, DM-009. Migrate AI comparison/status and neutral forms to roles, reduce compatibility selectors only after regression evidence. Preserve chart/tag/care identity and intentional print/light exceptions.\n4. **Visual direction:** DM-010. Apply the selected A/B/C direction after separate approval. Recheck mobile overflow, nested panels, dialogs, tooltip/menu layers, focus/hover/pressed, contrast, forced colors and reduced motion.\n5. **Release verification:** repeat the route gallery and conditional states; close sitter and live-agent gaps in an isolated environment. Compare light and dark desktop/mobile, perform keyboard and screen-reader passes, then document deploy scope. No schema or host configuration is proposed by this audit.\n''')
example={'auditVersion':1,'sourceCommit':commit,'decisions':[{'id':f['id'],'decision':'pending','note':''}for f in F]};(R/'review-decisions.example.json').write_text(json.dumps(example,indent=2))
data={'sourceCommit':commit,'counts':counts,'findings':F,'coverage':coverage,'palettes':states['palettes']}
